cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "OMEN: Open Movement and Exercise Nomenclature"
message: "If you use this standard or its reference encoder, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Carlos Abel"
    family-names: "Vivanco"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # add your ORCID iD
version: "0.1"
date-released: 2026-09-03
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  OMEN is a generative, computable naming standard for resistance-training
  movements. It describes a movement as a bundle of orthogonal facets, derives
  musculature from the movement pattern, and emits a canonical string plus a
  short, stable, versioned identifier suitable as a database primary key.
keywords:
  - resistance training
  - exercise nomenclature
  - controlled vocabulary
  - faceted classification
  - data interoperability
